<!--Q#-->
<exercise>
  <problem>
    <para>Daniel wants to surprise his girlfriend with a birthday party at her favorite restaurant. It will cost $42.75 per person for dinner, including tip and tax. His budget for the party is $500. Write an inequality to represent the maximum number of people, \( n \), Daniel can have at the party.</para>
    </problem><solution>
    
    <para>Enter your answer here:</para>
  
  <para>Compare your answer:</para>
    
    <para>\( 42.75n ≤ 500 \)</para>
  
  </solution></exercise>
